{"t": 1787314579.364, "kind": "message", "args": {"text": "Fixed. The root cause was `compute_checksum` using `ord(c)` (ordinal values) instead of each hex digit's value, contradicting the module's documented algorithm (`sum(payload hex digits) mod 16`).\n\nWith the corrected algorithm, all single-character tampering is reliably rejected: any one hex-digit change alters the sum by a non-zero amount mod 16, and the checksum digit itself is checked. The `None`/non-string and malformed cases were already handled by the `isinstance` guard. All tests pass."}, "raw_ref": 22}
